 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "You're building the tallest tower on Earth, in Dubai. So you set it on footings. Problem solved!",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But it weighs about four hundred fifty thousand tons, and the ground is weak, crumbly rock. It sinks.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you pour one giant concrete raft under the whole tower, to spread the weight.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But even spread out, that much weight keeps squeezing the weak rock below.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you drill one hundred ninety two piles, more than fifty meters down.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "There's no hard bottom to stand on, so the rubbing of the rock along each pile holds the tower up.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But the groundwater here is salty, and salt slowly eats concrete and steel.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you use extra dense concrete, plus a weak electric current that protects the steel.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Congratulations! You just built the foundation of the Burj Khalifa. What should we build next?",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
